23</fpage><lpage>129</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10785854</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dalymple</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Verga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The value of unenhanced helical computed tomography in the management of acute flank pain</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1998</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>735</fpage><lpage>774</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9474137</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Verga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenfield</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute ureteral obstruction: value of secondary signs of helical unenhanced CT</article-title><source>AJR</source><year>1996</year><volume>167</volume><fpage>1109</fpage><lpage>1113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8911160</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heneghan</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalrymple</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Verga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenfield</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Soft tissue "rim" sign in the diagnosis of ureteral calculi with use of unenhanced helical CT</article-title><source>Radio